From adefadc26ddb3186938925f645430a1bdb446b13 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kelsey <11334159+kernelzeroday@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 01:38:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] arm64: dts: qcom: glymur-asus-zenbook-a14: Limit the eDP
 link to HBR

The internal Samsung ATNA40CT06 panel trains successfully at HBR2 x2
(dp_debug reports rate=540000, num_lanes=2) and the DRM state looks
healthy, yet the panel stays completely dark. Capping the link at HBR
(2.7 Gbps per lane) gives a working picture.

1920x1200@60 needs ~3.7 Gbps at 24 bpp, which still fits in HBR x2.
The community A14 tree carries the same cap.

Signed-off-by: kelsey <11334159+kernelzeroday@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-asus-zenbook-a14-ux3407na.dts | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-asus-zenbook-a14-ux3407na.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-asus-zenbook-a14-ux3407na.dts
index fd6b8d8eb..6b8bed207 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-asus-zenbook-a14-ux3407na.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-asus-zenbook-a14-ux3407na.dts
@@ -713,7 +713,8 @@ edp_panel_in: endpoint {
 
 &mdss_dp3_out {
 	data-lanes = <0 1 2 3>;
-	link-frequencies = /bits/ 64 <1620000000 2700000000 5400000000 8100000000>;
+	/* The Samsung ATNA40CT06 OLED stays dark when trained at HBR2 */
+	link-frequencies = /bits/ 64 <1620000000 2700000000>;
 
 	remote-endpoint = <&edp_panel_in>;
 };
